Package: SSDTA
Type: Package
Title: Spectrum-Standardized Diagnostic Test Accuracy
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Samuel", "Schumacher", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "Schumacher.Samuel@gmail.com")
Author: Samuel Schumacher [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Samuel Schumacher <Schumacher.Samuel@gmail.com>
Description: Tools for spectrum-standardized diagnostic test accuracy. Estimate
    stratum-specific sensitivity across studies (Bayesian, GLMM, or conjugate
    engines), then reweight to a target population's burden distribution to
    obtain a standardized, context-specific sensitivity with propagation of
    posterior sensitivity uncertainty and Dirichlet case-mix sampling
    uncertainty, conditional on the chosen unobserved-stratum scenario. Useful
    in its own right for reporting expected sensitivity in a chosen population,
    and for comparing two tests without head-to-head data by differencing their
    standardized sensitivities under a common target distribution. When
    stratum-specific data are unavailable, an
    anchored difference-in-differences fallback partially deconfounds the
    comparison. The stratifier is generic (Xpert Ultra semi-quant for TB, but
    CD4 bands, Ct values, etc. for other settings). Implements the framework in
    Schumacher (2026) <doi:10.5281/zenodo.20033072>; see METHOD.md for the
    validity conditions, limitations and planned extensions.
URL: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20033072
